From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bryan Hoban <bryan.hoban@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 14:14:41 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Dolby Vision: display capabilities, DRM output state and
 diagnostics

What the window needs from the display and the DRM layer to put the
tunnel's signal up and take it down:

- Capabilities: DVBridgeEdid.h decides from the EDID whether a sink
  takes Standard (TV-led) Dolby Vision (v0, v1 and v2 VSVDBs; LLDV-only
  sinks are refused). It accepts HDMI Forum EEODB EDIDs, whose blocks
  outnumber byte 126, skips extension blocks with a bad checksum as DRM
  does, and takes a v0 block at its real length, 25 (edid-decode's
  "Version: 0 (26 bytes)" for the Vizio and Sharp v0 EDIDs in the
  linuxhw/EDID collection; Amlogic's HDMI driver accepts v0 only with
  length 0x19). It is MIT and must stay identical to the kernel's copy
  (linux-9902, dvbridge_edid.h). CDisplayInfo also reports the desired
  maximum luminance and the HDR10+ VSVDB's application version.
- CDVBridgeState captures the connector and CRTC properties the tunnel
  changes (DVBRIDGE_TUNNEL_FORMAT, HDR_OUTPUT_METADATA, Colorspace,
  Broadcast RGB, max bpc, the colour pipeline, VRR_ENABLED, ...),
  stages the Dolby Vision, HDR10 or HDR10+ signal and restores SDR.
- CDRMAtomic commits a Dolby Vision page transactionally
  (FlipPageTransactional, with the GBM surface's transactional buffers
  in GBMUtils): a refused commit never replaces the scanout. A failing
  HDMI output is retried twice at once, then every 250 ms for three
  seconds and every second after that (DVBridgeOutputRetry), never
  excluded for good; the restore is always attempted. Once a scanout
  has been accepted its pictures commit without ALLOW_MODESET. With
  DV_PRIVATE_NONBLOCK=1 a picture of a stable scanout is committed
  NONBLOCK with an out-fence, one flip at a time (WaitDVFlip,
  WaitDVRefresh); the flips are counted and logged every 600
  (DV_PRIVATE_FLIP_TRACE=1 logs each). It ships off: it could not be
  tested without a display.
- CWinSystemGbm: SupportsNativeDVOutput, FlipDVBridgePage, the
  display's peak brightness and HDR10+ version, and CompleteModeset, so
  that the refresh change for a native stream can ride on the bridge's
  first commit (one HDMI change instead of two).
- The whitelist search lets a native Dolby Vision stream (and only it)
  use a mode at its exact progressive rate (allowNativeProgressiveRates).
- DRMUtils: the opaque framebuffer of a buffer made without modifiers
  (amdgpu).
- Diagnostics in kodi.log without debug logging: bounded first-failure
  and change reports, accepted signal changes and recent kernel Dolby
  Vision rejection reasons, copied in a background job
  (DVBridgeDiagnosticState, DVBridgeKernelLog, DVBridgeKernelLogReader;
  yblod-engine/docs/intel-dv/DIAGNOSTICS.md). Their counters never
  drive playback decisions. DVBRIDGE_DIAGNOSTICS=0 turns them off; =1
  also asks for the playback health line (kodi-9955).

Used by the window in kodi-9957. DVBridgeState.cpp reads the output mode
from DVOutputSettings.h, which kodi-9955 adds: the Dolby Vision patches
are one unit that builds only as a whole. Formerly the DRM, GBM and
display parts of kodi-9990-native-dv, kodi-9994-hdmi-recovery,
kodi-9995-diagnostics, kodi-9996-output-modes-and-info,
kodi-9999-dv-single-modeset, yblod-03, -07 (SDR restore), -26 (amdgpu
opaque framebuffer), -28 (stable commit), -31 (HDR10 through the
tunnel), -32, -34 (HDR10+), -43 and -49 (the DRM side of held pictures
and queued flips), -52 (EEODB and v0 EDIDs) and -57 (diagnostics cost).
